<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageType>Template</PackageType>
    <PackageId>GPreviatti.Template.Hexagonal.Solution</PackageId>
    <Title>Hexagonal architecture solution template</Title>
    <Authors>Giovanni Brunno Previatti</Authors>
    <Description>Solution following Hexagonal architecture and best practices.</Description>
    <PackageTags>template;hexagonal-architecture;clean-architecture;ddd;blazor;webui;net10</PackageTags>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IncludeContentInPack>true</IncludeContentInPack>
    <IncludeBuildOutput>false</IncludeBuildOutput>
    <ContentTargetFolders>content</ContentTargetFolders>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU5128</NoWarn>
    <NoDefaultExcludes>true</NoDefaultExcludes>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/gpreviatti/hexagonal-solution-template</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>Readme.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>git://github.com/gpreviatti/hexagonal-solution-template</RepositoryUrl>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
    - Rename CLAUDE.md to AGENTS.md in all templates (Bff, Contracts, Full, Simple, SimpleWebUi, WebUi) for compatibility with other AI agents.
    - Move detailed agent guidance (code examples, configuration, and step-by-step guides) from AGENTS.md into each template's Readme.md, keeping AGENTS.md to rules and links.
    - Fix broken references in the agent guidance: missing guide files, wrong project paths, and a nonexistent Stryker config.
    - Add the release agent skill (.github/skills/release).
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="templates\**\*" Exclude="templates\**\bin\**;templates\**\obj\**" />
    <Compile Remove="**\*" />
    <None Include="Readme.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>